1
00:00:05,070 --> 00:00:07,370
- Okay, see you later.
- Good news.

2
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:10,770
(Sheldon:)I finally have a handle on my
idea for three-person chess.

3
00:00:12,110 --> 00:00:14,960
(Leonard:)That is good news. Bye.

4
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,130
(Sheldon:)Uh, do you know
how I solved

5
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:18,900
the balanced center
combat-area problem?

6
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:20,250
Five words:

7
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:24,500
(Sheldon:)transitional quadrilateral
to triangular tessellation.

8
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:27,640
(Leonard:)That... that's brilliant.

9
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:29,680
(Sheldon:)It's what I do.

10
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:31,930
(Sheldon:)But wait, there's more.

11
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:34,880
(Sheldon:)I also invented
two new chess pieces.

12
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:38,080
(Sheldon:)The serpent...
and the old woman.

13
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:42,690
(Leonard:)Okay, now I have to ask.
What do they do?

14
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:45,720
(Sheldon:)When the serpent slithers
to an opposing player's piece,

15
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:47,790
(Sheldon:)that piece
is considered poisoned

16
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:51,060
(Sheldon:)and will die
after two more moves.

17
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,800
(Leonard:)All right.

18
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,600
(Sheldon:)Unless... it gets to
the old woman in time,

19
00:00:58,610 --> 00:01:01,270
(Sheldon:)in which case
she sucks out the poison,

